{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh: keep completed work free of false merge blockers.\n\nThe thread spine currently adds a red **open** branch saying “a merge refuses it until the behaviour is re-anchored” whenever the selected approval carries the superseded-world flag. It does not check whether the commitment is already complete or when the world moved. The [warning code](ui/src/lib/spine.ts@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:348) therefore turns historical provenance into an instruction to do more work.\n\nI reproduced this with the current reader projection at #19966 and the actual UI rendering function. Toolbar request #16429 is satisfied and landed, with approval #16654 and its first moved-world cause at #16672. Notes request #19022 is also satisfied and landed, with approval #19118 and cause #19153. Both get the red open branch. Clearing only that flag in a cloned projection removes it. Their landings remain recorded throughout. The attached `spine-warning-evidence.json` preserves both exact lifecycles, dates and rendering results. This was a read-only rendering probe, not a new interactive browser test.\n\nThe wording also contradicts the [dated merge rule](docs/reference/gs/merge.md@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:96): a world that moved after the verdict is recorded; a cause already present at the verdict, or one that cannot be dated, is a refusal. The flag alone does not establish that a merge must refuse. Other guards can still refuse a particular head; the browser should not claim permission either.\n\n**Recommended small repair:** use the existing commitment lifecycle to keep closed work free of live-action blockers. Keep the provenance flag visible as history, with its cause and date where available. On active work, describe the observed changed basis and link to the governing explanation; do not infer a full merge verdict from one flag or copy the merge authority logic into the browser. Preserve all source-landing and approved-artifact accounting evidence.\n\nReplace the [current flag-only test](ui/test/interaction.test.mjs@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:931) with cases for completed landing, accepted completion without a merge, and an active approval whose cause is before, after or undated relative to its verdict. Verify the actual displayed branch, wording and links; retain refusal evidence without inventing an open obligation or a green permission signal. Exercise one completed and one active thread in the browser.\n\nThis is a separate, bounded presentation correction alongside #19939: it changes neither P2 lifecycle semantics nor the independent landing audit, and needs no new workflow state, event, historical retirement or repeat review of completed work. I recommend it as a high-impact way to reduce unnecessary investigation and rework; this note is for your review, not an adopted policy.","body":{"head":"07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:765878117cb1813fae8925e4dd84dc5955ec94f9, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7893c91807f71c18e1334b106bbded3b26c6d410, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7ad707636e1123e18dc102bc24672bf4d9c1937c stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0fae00055767520da097d824d3f7732892d47ef8, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:207fceae71ec15f3f8e1d046517d1a4f446532bd, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:27bb6f88608eacd78b92df36e0bac34c3ccef304 and 40 more"}}